---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import TopNav from '../../components/TopNav.astro';
import { authoredWidth } from '../../lib/authoredWidth';

const kbImg = '24-pipeforge-kb-first-rule-2026-10-02.png';

// Each panel: image filename in /screenshots, a short section label, alt text
// and a one-line caption. Kept in execution order.
const panels = [
  {
    section: 'Planning',
    img: '03-execution-order-dependency-graph.png',
    alt: 'Chunk dependency graph: backend foundation → tests + 3 independent frontends',
    caption: 'Planner splits an epic into chunks and marks what runs in parallel after the foundation.',
  },
  {
    section: 'Plan review',
    img: '11-plan-reviewer-findings-classification.png',
    alt: 'Plan review finishes with 5 severity-classified findings + a graceful proceed prompt',
    caption: 'Plan reviewed before any code: 5 findings, each with a concrete fix.',
  },
  {
    section: 'Execution',
    img: '02-parallel-chunks-group1-complete.png',
    alt: '8 agents in parallel: Group 1 light reviews + Group 2 implementers',
    caption: '8 agents at once: Group 2 implementers plus light reviewers for Group 1.',
  },
  {
    section: 'Heavy review',
    img: '14-heavy-review-complete-findings-table.png',
    alt: '5 reviewers, 34 findings, 0 critical, clean to merge',
    caption: '5 review agents, 34 findings, 0 critical. Derived from the open-source pr-review-toolkit.',
  },
  {
    section: 'Fidelity audit',
    img: '15-fidelity-auditor-critical-drift-caught.png',
    alt: 'A real regression caught: flash key silently unified across two flows',
    caption: 'Fidelity auditor catches a silent UX regression in a refactor: 20/21 OK, 1 critical.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Pipeforge + Fleetforge · sebrogala.dev"
  description="Pipeforge and Fleetforge: orchestration for Claude Code and Codex on a PostgreSQL MCP server, with a screenshot walkthrough of real runs."
>
  <TopNav current="projects" />

  <main class="frame">
    <header class="page-header">
      <div class="eyebrow">Walkthrough</div>
      <h1>Pipeforge + Fleetforge</h1>
      <p class="lede">Orchestration for Claude Code and Codex on a PostgreSQL MCP server, with Fleetforge as the coordinator layer across projects. The Education SaaS, OMS and ProfitOfExile all ship through them. Both are private tools I use daily, not products.</p>
      <p class="sub-lede">Public tracker IDs (<code>POE-###</code>) stay visible in the screenshots. Private ones are replaced with <code>[TSK-000]</code>.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>How it runs</h2>
      <p>Agent sessions run in four levels: coordinator (Fleetforge), supervisor, orchestrators and implementers. Questions escalate one level at a time, and sessions hand over at a set context threshold.</p>
      <p>That setup carried the first long run, in 09.2026: about four days across three projects, in two stretches. On the client system alone it landed 73 reviewed work items in about 56 active hours.</p>
      <p>I pick the models with blind A/B tests on real work items, using hidden tests and blind cross-vendor judges. In 09.2026 Claude Opus 5.5 (low) replaced GPT-6 Luna as implementer, at 2–8× the speed with equal results. GPT-6 Sol stayed as reviewer, so no model checks its own work.</p>
      <p>Review also runs through custom auditor agents for fidelity, delivery, security and architecture. I added the fidelity auditor after an AI silently cut a 491-line spec to 122 lines. It checks that behaviour survives moves and splits, and I use it on refactors and AI meta-work, not as a constant guard.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose" id="knowledge-base">
      <h2>Knowledge base</h2>
      <p>Pipeforge's own design decisions go into a knowledge base, each with its rationale, rejected alternatives and source files, written at the moment of decision. It exists so I stop re-explaining why something works the way it does. For now it covers Pipeforge itself.</p>
      <figure class="panel-figure" style={`max-width:${authoredWidth(kbImg)}px`}>
        <a
          href={`/screenshots/${kbImg}`}
          class="lightbox-link"
          aria-label="Open full-size screenshot"
        >
          <img
            src={`/screenshots/${kbImg}`}
            alt="Pipeforge's CLAUDE.md in an editor. KB-first rule: call queryKnowledge() or listKnowledgeConcepts() via MCP as the first action whenever a prompt names a skill, agent, manifest, gate, contract, route, pipeline type or worker, contains terms such as autonomy, dispatch, orchestrator or triage, asks how or why something works, or proposes editing plugin files. Code exploration fills gaps after the KB, not before. KB degradation heuristic: after the KB call on a single-concept question, check whether the KB alone gave a correct, complete answer, and if not, write or enrich the entry"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </a>
        <figcaption>Pipeforge's CLAUDE.md: agents check the KB first and fill gaps when it falls short.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    {
      panels.map((p, i) => (
        <section class="panel">
          <div class="panel-meta">
            <div class="panel-num">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</div>
            <div class="panel-section-label">{p.section}</div>
          </div>
          <figure class="panel-figure" style={`max-width:${authoredWidth(p.img)}px`}>
            <a
              href={`/screenshots/${p.img}`}
              class="lightbox-link"
              aria-label="Open full-size screenshot"
            >
              <img
                src={`/screenshots/${p.img}`}
                alt={p.alt}
                loading="lazy"
                decoding="async"
              />
            </a>
            <figcaption>{p.caption}</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </section>
      ))
    }

    <footer class="page-footer">
      <a href="/">← back home</a>
      <span class="sep">·</span>
      <a href="/projects">↑ projects</a>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .frame {
    max-width: 1140px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 48px 32px;
  }
  /* Content blocks span the full frame width (matching Home). If specific
     long-form paragraphs need narrower line lengths for readability, cap
     them individually — not at the section level. */

  /* Topnav lives in src/components/TopNav.astro. */
  /* `.sep` is also used in the page footer below — keep as page-level rule. */
  .sep {
    color: var(--rule-2);
  }

  .page-header {
    margin-bottom: 36px;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.78125rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 3.03125rem;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .lede {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.3125rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--fg);
    text-wrap: pretty;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .sub-lede {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.96875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--fg-nav);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .sub-lede code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--fg-nav);
    background: var(--bg-raise);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }


  .prose {
    margin: 32px 0 36px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .prose h3 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.15625rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin: 28px 0 10px;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  }
  .prose p + p,
  .prose p + ul,
  .prose ul + p {
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
  .prose p + .panel-figure {
    margin-top: 20px;
  }
  .prose ul {
    padding-left: 22px;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .prose li:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .prose em {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .prose code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.90625rem;
    color: var(--fg-nav);
    background: var(--bg-raise);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .prose strong {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .prose a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-color: rgba(125, 179, 108, 0.4);
  }

  .panel {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: 36px 0;
  }
  .panel-meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }
  .panel-num {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .panel-section-label {
    color: var(--muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }
  .panel-figure {
    /* Capped inline at the capture's authored width; the caption is a child of
       the same element, so it matches the image width exactly. */
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .panel-figure a {
    display: block;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule-2);
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--bg-raise);
    transition: border-color 160ms ease;
  }
  .panel-figure a:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .panel-figure img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  .panel-figure figcaption {
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--fg-nav);
    text-wrap: pretty;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .page-footer {
    margin-top: 48px;
    padding-top: 22px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.90625rem;
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .page-footer a {
    color: var(--accent);
    transition: color 160ms ease;
  }
  .page-footer a:hover {
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .frame {
      padding: 36px 22px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: 2.1875rem;
    }
    .lede {
      font-size: 1.09375rem;
    }
    .sub-lede {
      font-size: 0.90625rem;
    }


    .panel {
      padding: 28px 0;
    }
    .panel-figure figcaption {
      font-size: 0.90625rem;
    }
  }
</style>
</Base>
